   "evidence": "Standard.lean: `theorem ker_map_dualRestrict_augmentation (h : IsUnit (Fintype.card \u03c3 : K))`. `h` is used only through `augmentationProjection \u03c3 h`, which is built from `ofMulActionEquivProdAugmentation \u2026 h`. The math: `v \u2212 (\u2211\u2c7c v\u2c7c)\u00b7single i\u2080 1 \u2208 V\u2080` is a `K`-linear retraction onto `V\u2080` over any ring.",
   "file": "TauCeti/RepresentationTheory/SymmetricAlgebra/Standard.lean",
   "fix": "Remove `h` from the kernel theorem. For surjectivity, use the section `\u03c8 \u21a6 \u03c8 \u2218 (v \u21a6 v \u2212 (\u2211 coeffs v) \u2022 single i\u2080 1)`, or the complement `K\u00b7single i\u2080 1`. Then drop `h` from the injectivity lemma, keep it only for surjectivity and the equivalence, and update the docstrings to match.",
   "issue": "The public `ker_map_dualRestrict_augmentation` (and the private `mem_span_sumCoords_of_dualRestrict_eq_zero` it uses) assume `h : IsUnit (Fintype.card \u03c3 : K)`, but the kernel is `(e\u2081)` over every commutative ring. `V\u2080` has the complement `K\u00b7single i\u2080 1` for any `i\u2080 : \u03c3` (if `\u03c3` is empty, both sides are trivially zero), so restriction is always surjective, and a form vanishing on every `x\u1d62 \u2212 x\u2c7c` is a multiple of `sumCoords`. As a result, the algebraic independence of the restricted `e\u2082, \u2026, e_(n+1)` (`injective_esymmStandardAlgHom`) also needs no unit hypothesis.",
   "line": 165
  }
